VeridianOS: fix compiler warnings in plasma-workspace

GCC warnings fixed at the cause (no suppression). Behaviour is unchanged
except where noted.

- -Wunused-parameter: unnamed in klipper ActionsWidget::onItemChanged (col),
  ksecretprompter UnlockCollectionPrompt/CreateCollectionPrompt
  (activationToken, D-Bus API), PromptContext's serviceUnregistered lambda
  (serviceName), ksmserver sanity_check (argc, argv), PanelView's
  editModeChanged lambda (edit), ShellCorona's checkUiReady lambda (visible)
  and Notifications::showInhibitionSummary (blacklistedDesktopEntries,
  blacklistedNotifyRcNames; public Q_INVOKABLE API, the parameters are not
  used by the implementation). [[maybe_unused]] where the parameter is used
  only under a build option: Unit::getLastJournalEntries (unit,
  HAVE_SYSTEMD), kicker handleAppstreamActions (service, HAVE_APPSTREAMQT),
  MediaMetadata::read (path, HAVE_KExiv2).
- -Wunused-variable / -Wunused-but-set-variable: freespacenotifier tested
  `auto volume = device.as<StorageVolume>()` only for non-null; it now uses
  the equivalent device.is<StorageVolume>(). The ksecretprompter test keeps
  creating its self-registering Request object without the unused pointer.
  Dead counters removed in kfontinst Folder::list (i) and
  CFontFileList::run (n), and the dead flag oldSystrayInstantiated in
  SystemTray.
- -Wunused-function / -Wunused-variable in ksmserver/server.cpp: the
  unused helper fprintfhex() and the unused static remTempFile removed.
- -Wunused-function in logout-greeter: systemdUpdateTriggerFileInfo() and the
  PackageKit file-name constants are used only under
  PACKAGEKIT_OFFLINE_UPDATES; they are now defined under the same condition.
- -Wreorder: KSMShutdownDlg's constructor initialises m_windowed before
  m_result, matching the declaration order (the values do not depend on
  each other).
- -Wparentheses in ksmserver/server.cpp: the intended assignment in
  `if (file_entry->auth_data = malloc(...))` gets the extra parentheses.
- -Wrestrict in ksmserver/legacy.cpp: select() was given the same fd_set as
  readfds and exceptfds, which are restrict-qualified, so the kernel's
  results for both sets were written to one object (undefined behaviour per
  the prototype). Two separate sets with the same fd are passed now; the
  result is still not inspected, the call only waits for activity or the
  timeout as before.
- -Wimplicit-fallthrough in kicker AppEntry::init: case NameOnly set
  m_description and fell into NameAndGenericName, which sets the same
  m_description again. The two cases are merged, which is what the code did.
- -Wswitch in PanelView's locationChanged handler: Floating, Desktop and
  FullScreen are not screen edges, so no form factor follows from them;
  they are listed explicitly and keep the form factor, as before.
- -Wdeprecated-declarations:
  * LayerShellQt::Shell::useLayerShell() ("not needed since Qt 6.5"): it
    only set QT_WAYLAND_SHELL_INTEGRATION=layer-shell process-wide. The
    splash windows already request the layer-shell role per window with
    LayerShellQt::Window::get(), the replacement since Qt 6.5, so the call
    and its now-empty SplashApp::setupWaylandIntegration() are removed.
  * QString::fromUcs4(const uint *, qsizetype) in kfontinst CharTip: the
    code point is passed as char32_t.
- -Wunused-result (QFile::open, [[nodiscard]]):
  * startplasma: a missing kdedefaults/package file already meant "apply
    the defaults" unless the look-and-feel name is empty (readLine() on the
    unopened file returned nothing); an unopened file now reads as empty
    without calling readLine(), which keeps that behaviour exactly and
    stops Qt's "device not open" warning.
  * KLookAndFeelManager::save: writing kdedefaults/package now happens only
    when the open succeeded, and a failure is reported with qWarning() as
    elsewhere in libklookandfeel (it was silently lost before).
- musl "#warning redirecting incorrect #include <sys/errno.h>" (kfontinst
  dbus/Helper.cpp) and "<sys/poll.h>" (libtaskmanager
  waylandtasksmodel.cpp): include the POSIX <errno.h> and <poll.h>.

